      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Hmm... this causes the PS_RDY to be sent as a sink. Should it be in PD_STATE_SRC_SWAP_STANDBY?\n\nThis is intentional. Port role is generally supposed to follow the Rd/Rp applied.\n\nPR_SWAP -\u003e ACCEPT -\u003e GOODCRC\n\n[Former source shuts off Vbus, applies Rd]\nSNK:DFP PS_RDY#1 (\u003c\u003d\u003d your observation, note former SRC is expressing Rd here)\nSNK:UFP GoodCRC\n\n[Former sink raises Vbus, applies Rp]\nSRC:UFP PS_RDY#2\nSNK:DFP GoodCRC\n\n\nThis is explained in the spec in 7.3.9 and 7.3.10. Please note Step 3 happens before Step 4.\n\n3\n[......] The power supply informs the Device Policy Manager that it is ready to operate as the new Sink. The CC termination is changed from Rp to Rd (see [USB Type-C 1.3]). The power supply status is passed to the Policy Engine.\n[\u003c\u003d\u003d Policy Manager is now in SNK mode, is expressing Rd]\n\n4\nThe Policy Engine sends the PS_RDY Message to the soon to be new Source.\n[\u003c\u003d\u003d Therefore PS_RDY#1 sent as SNK]",
